The smoke test and rendering checks pass, but the new list-valued insert feature has incorrect positioning for non-overlay elements.

Review comment:

- [P2] Stack multiple inserts instead of reusing one position — C:/Users/NR SMART/tools/lcdg-reel/lcdg/inserts.py:1674-1677
  When a block provides `insert` as a list with multiple elements without `sur`, every insert is constructed with the same `bas`, so they receive identical coordinates and render on top of one another. This contradicts the documented list behavior that elements should stack; update the placement baseline after each non-overlay insert.
